<%- include('partials/head') %>
<div class="container narrow">
  <h1 style="margin:24px 0 8px">How <%= site.name %> works</h1>
  <p class="muted">A simple, free lost-and-found board for everyone at <%= site.college %>, built and run by the <%= site.poweredBy %>.</p>

  <div class="panel stack">
    <div>
      <h2><span class="tag tag-lost">Lost</span> If you lost something</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Tap <strong>I lost something</strong>, describe it and add a photo if you have one.</li>
        <li>Everyone who has notifications on is alerted. Share the post on your class WhatsApp group too.</li>
        <li>If someone has it, they tap <strong>I found this</strong>. You get a notification.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Yes, that's mine</strong> and you'll both see each other's mobile number. Call or WhatsApp to meet.</li>
        <li>Got it back? Tap <strong>I got it back</strong> to close the post.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2><span class="tag tag-found">Found</span> If you found something</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Tap <strong>I found something</strong>, take a photo, and say where it is: with you, or deposited at a collection point (e.g. the department office).</li>
        <li>Add a <strong>secret detail</strong> that only the real owner would know. Only you and admins see it.</li>
        <li>The owner taps <strong>This is mine</strong> and describes it. If it matches, confirm and numbers are shared.</li>
        <li>Hand it over (ask to see their college ID), then mark it <strong>Returned</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Good to know</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your number is private.</strong> It's only shown to the other person after a match is confirmed.</li>
        <li><strong>Posts close automatically</strong>: lost posts after <%= config.LOST_EXPIRY_DAYS %> days, found posts after <%= config.FOUND_EXPIRY_DAYS %> days. You get a reminder before that and can extend <%= config.MAX_EXTENSIONS %> times.</li>
        <li>You can close your own post any time. Admins can close or remove posts that break the rules.</li>
        <li>Unclaimed found items should be deposited with the department office.</li>
        <li>Never pay anyone to "return" an item. Report misuse to the admins.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Notifications on iPhone</h2>
      <p class="small">Open this site in Safari, tap <em>Share → Add to Home Screen</em>, open it from the home screen and then turn on notifications.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
